        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="463"><label>taken from</label> <ref target="clause:IIIEg_8">III Eg 8</ref> <quote>This section is taken from VI Ethelred, 32, 32.1 (cf. V. 26.1), the latter clause being itself from III Edgar, 8.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="463"><label>taken from</label> <ref target="clause:VAtr_26-1">V Atr 26.1</ref> <quote>This section is taken from VI Ethelred, 32, 32.1 (cf. V. 26.1), the latter clause being itself from III Edgar, 8.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="463"><label>taken from</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_32">VI Atr 32–32.1</ref> <quote>This section is taken from VI Ethelred, 32, 32.1 (cf. V. 26.1), the latter clause being itself from III Edgar, 8.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="334"><label>recurs in later code</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_32">VI Atr 32–32.2</ref> <quote>Almost all these additions recurred in codes later drafted by Wulfstan for Cnut (n. 332: VI Atr 32–32.2, Cn 1018 20.1–21, II Cn 8, II Cn 9)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#kennedy" n="59"><label>used in I–II Cnut</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-055">Cn 1018 20–20.2</ref> <quote>Kennedy’s table: VI Æthelred 31–32.1 | D 20–20.2 | II Cnut 8</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">‘ymbe’ is probably to be supplied in G before ‘feos’ (B ‘ymbe’, A and Ld ‘embe’, Consiliatio). B's heading ‘Feos bote’ is red in the margin. Liebermann compares VI Atr 31–32.1; III Eg 8.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 315, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
